  "card": "This PR caps the -bytespersigop startup option to [0, 21474] and moves the mempool standard sigop limit check before changeset staging. Currently, negative or large -bytespersigop values cause arithmetic overflow in mempool int32_t size metrics, and transactions with extreme sigop counts trigger overflows during staging before their standardness is evaluated. These overflows abort debug builds on internal Assume assertions in fee calculation and transaction graph logic. The change requires no external dependencies.",
